# b1-innsbruck-retreat: the battle of session 9 (Innsbruck, 1805), played by the Allies, who
# defend. The player retreats with F9 at the first unit's order and answers Yes.
# One keys file for the PDS 7.1 build in DOSBox-X (tools/play/play.py --napoleon) and the
# QB64 builds (tests/play.py tactical). The battle's BATTLE.$$$ is b1-innsbruck-retreat.battle.
# seed 1 (NAP_SEED)

# A TICK of a second or more: any key ends it. A "hit a key" pause: a space.
rule 3 key f12
rule 1 key space
play until 5
# shot first-order
state
key f9
play until 2:R
# shot retreat-ask
state
text y
# over writes OUTCOME.&&& and waits at place 7 before it exits (scriptend).
play until 7:O
# shot result
state
key f12
